Generating first stage environment...
  Rationale: Stage 1: The absolute simplest starting point. The cube spawns at the exact center of the table (zero randomization) and reward shaping is enabled. On top of the default shaped reward, we add substantial bonus rewards for partial progress: (1) a proximity bonus that ramps up as the gripper gets very close, (2) a touch/contact bonus for any gripper-cube contact, (3) a grasp bonus, (4) a lift-progress bonus that rewards any upward movement of the cube, and (5) a large success bonus. The short horizon (200 steps) means episodes cycle quickly, giving the agent many attempts. The cube is always in the same spot, so the agent only needs to learn a single reach-grasp-lift trajectory. With dense shaping and a fixed target, even random exploration should stumble into partial rewards almost immediately.
  Timesteps: 500,000
  Validating environment...
