Generating first stage environment...
  Rationale: Stage 1: Absolute simplest environment to bootstrap learning. The cube is placed at the exact center of the table (zero spawn range) with reward shaping enabled. On top of that, we add substantial bonus rewards for partial progress milestones:

1. Reaching reward (from robosuite's built-in shaping) - rewards getting close to the cube
2. Grasp bonus - extra reward when the gripper grasps the cube
3. Lifting bonus - continuous reward proportional to how high the cube is lifted above the table
4. Success bonus - big reward for full success

The cube is always at the same position, so the agent only needs to learn a single reach trajectory. This dramatically reduces exploration complexity. A randomly initialized policy should stumble into reaching the cube quickly since it's always at the same spot near the robot's home position. The dense shaping rewards ensure every small improvement is reinforced.

We also use a shorter horizon (200 steps) to get more resets per timestep budget, which means more opportunities to practice the beginning of the trajectory. 500k timesteps should be sufficient to learn reliable reaching and grasping at the fixed position.
  Timesteps: 500,000
  Validating environment...
