Generating stage 1 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 0 results show the agent learned well - rewards peaked around 40 at 250k steps then declined slightly, suggesting some overfitting or instability but solid learning of the fixed-position task. The rewards are high (30-40 range with bonus rewards), indicating the agent can reliably reach, grasp, and lift the cube at the center position.

For Stage 1, I'll introduce a small amount of cube spawn randomization (±0.02m, slightly less than the default ±0.03m) to start generalizing the learned behavior. I'll keep the same bonus reward structure but slightly reduce the extra bonuses since the agent already knows the basic skill. I'll also increase the horizon to 250 steps to give slightly more time for the potentially harder task. The key changes are:
1. Cube spawns in a small region around center (±0.02m) instead of exactly at center
2. Slight rotation randomization added
3. Horizon increased to 250 to accommodate the slightly harder positioning
4. Keep reward shaping and bonus rewards to maintain learning signal
  Timesteps: 500,000
  Validating environment...
