============================================================
STAGE 2
============================================================
Generating stage 2 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 1 results show strong performance - rewards reached ~45 by the end and were still trending upward slightly, with low std_reward (~2.24) indicating consistent success. The agent has mastered the ±0.02m spawn range well.

For Stage 2, I'll increase the cube spawn range to ±0.06m (double the default ±0.03m range), which is a moderate step up from ±0.02m. This forces the agent to generalize its reaching behavior to a wider area. I'll also increase the horizon to 300 steps to give more time for reaching cubes that are farther away. I'll keep the same bonus reward structure since it's been working well, but slightly reduce the grasp bonus to start weaning the agent off the extra scaffolding. The key goal here is spatial generalization - the agent needs to learn to reach and lift the cube from a variety of positions, not just near center.
  Timesteps: 750,000
  Validating environment...
