Generating stage 3 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 2 results show good but somewhat variable performance - rewards oscillated between ~50-70 with moderate standard deviations (6-24), suggesting the agent has learned the ±0.06m range reasonably well but hasn't fully saturated. The rewards plateaued around 60-70 in the later checkpoints rather than continuing to climb.

For Stage 3, I'll increase the spawn range to ±0.10m, which is a meaningful step toward the practical table bounds (~±0.15m). This is a moderate increase from ±0.06m. I'll also increase the horizon to 400 steps to give more time for reaching cubes that are further away. I'll continue reducing the bonus rewards slightly to wean the agent toward the native robosuite reward structure, but keep them present since the task is getting harder. The gradual reduction of bonuses across stages ensures the agent doesn't become too dependent on the scaffolding rewards.
  Timesteps: 750,000
