Generating stage 4 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 3 results show highly variable performance - rewards oscillated between ~29-76 with large standard deviations (11-37), indicating inconsistent success at the ±0.10m spawn range. The mean rewards haven't clearly improved over the 750k steps (started ~39, ended ~62, but with lots of variance). The agent seems to have partially learned but is struggling with consistency.

For Stage 4, rather than pushing to even wider spawn ranges, I'll keep the same ±0.10m range but make some adjustments to help the agent consolidate its learning:
1. Keep ±0.10m spawn range (same as Stage 3) - the agent needs more practice at this level before going wider
2. Increase horizon to 500 to give more time per episode for harder cube positions
3. Slightly increase bonus rewards back up to help the agent get more consistent at this range
4. Add a distance-based bonus that provides continuous reward signal for approaching the cube, which helps with the wider spawn positions

The idea is to strengthen the agent's performance at the current difficulty before pushing further. The extra time per episode and slightly stronger reward signal should help reduce the variance we saw in Stage 3.
