Generating stage 4 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 3 results show highly variable performance - rewards oscillate between ~29 and ~76 with large standard deviations (often 20-33), and the mean reward has roughly plateaued around 55-62 without clear upward trend. The high variance suggests the agent succeeds on some cube positions but fails on others within the ±0.10m range. Simply continuing training is unlikely to help much given the plateau pattern.

For Stage 4, instead of increasing the spawn range further, I'll keep the same ±0.10m spawn range but focus on consolidating performance with a longer horizon (500 steps) and slightly stronger reward shaping to reduce the variance. I'll also add a distance-based bonus that provides a smoother gradient for reaching, which should help the agent handle edge cases better. The bonus rewards will remain at similar levels to Stage 3 since the agent still needs the scaffolding at this difficulty level. Once performance is more consistent at ±0.10m, we can push to wider ranges in the next stage.

Key changes from Stage 3:
1. Same spawn range (±0.10m) but with enhanced reaching reward shaping
2. Horizon increased to 500 for more exploration time
3. Added a continuous reaching bonus on top of robosuite's built-in shaping to provide stronger gradient
4. Slightly increased grasp and lift bonuses back up to help stabilize learning
